---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Neighborhood
description: Where the Kennedy-King neighborhood is, the parks and trails inside it, and what it's like to live here on the near north side of Indianapolis.
heading: Our neighborhood
lead: A small, walkable neighborhood just north of downtown Indianapolis, between 16th and 22nd Streets.
---
{% from "partials/macros.njk" import ext %}

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="where-title">
  <div class="container split split--media-right">
    {# TODO: map from King Park Development Corporation. Confirm permission or replace. #}
    <figure class="split__media">
      <img src="/images/king-park-map.webp" width="750" height="807" loading="lazy"
           alt="Map of the King Park area. Kennedy-King runs from 16th Street north to 22nd Street, between Central Avenue and the Monon Trail, with MLK Park inside it.">
      <figcaption>Map: King Park Development Corporation</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <h2 id="where-title">Where we are</h2>
      <p>Kennedy-King sits on the near north side, a short walk or ride from downtown.</p>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>South:</strong> 16th Street</li>
        <li><strong>North:</strong> 22nd Street</li>
        <li><strong>East:</strong> the Monon Trail</li>
        <li><strong>West:</strong> Central Avenue</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Park sits inside those lines, and we're part of the wider King Park area of neighborhoods.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="places-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <h2 id="places-title">Parks and trails</h2>
        <p>All of them are free, and open dawn to dusk.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {# Places come from _data/places.yml #}
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--2">
      {%- for place in places %}
      <article class="card">
        <h3>{% if place.url %}{{ ext(place.url, place.name) }}{% else %}{{ place.name }}{% endif %}</h3>
        <p>{{ place.summary }}</p>
        {%- if place.address %}<p class="card__meta">{{ place.address }}</p>{%- endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="living-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="living-title">Living here</h2>
    {# TODO: draft copy, drawn from the old About page. #}
    <p>The neighborhood dates back to the 1800s and is rich in architectural history. It's one of the city's fastest growing urban neighborhoods, and still a quiet one: under a thousand residents in fewer than four hundred households, where people know the names of the folks on their block.</p>
    <p>Neighbors meet on the last Monday of each month, and the association organizes clean-ups, block parties, and get-togethers through the year. <a href="/get-involved/">Everyone is welcome to take part</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="partners-title">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 id="partners-title">Who we work with</h2>
    {# Partners come from _data/partners.yml, listed alphabetically #}
    <div class="card-grid">
      {%- for p in partners | sort(false, false, "name") %}
      <article class="card">
        <h3>{% if p.url %}{{ ext(p.url, p.name) }}{% else %}{{ p.name }}{% endif %}</h3>
        <p>{{ p.summary }}</p>
        {%- if p.link %}<p class="card__meta">{{ ext(p.link.url, p.link.label) }}</p>{%- endif %}
        {%- if p.note %}<p class="card__meta"><a href="{{ p.note.url }}">{{ p.note.label }}</a></p>{%- endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
